                <pb facs="0326" n="256" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg256"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/3797: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-06-05T15:00:00+01:00">June 5, 1934—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 5—11:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>136. Arms embargo. Consulate’s 135, June 5,2 p.m., paragraph 3. I have been
                    privately informed that a meeting of “interested states” was also considered
                    with thought being given to possible American participation. There have been no
                    outward developments in this whatsoever and I have heard no discussion of
                    it.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
